# Environment variables

Every value has a working local default. Copy this file to `.env` (or export the
variables) to override.

## Storage

```bash
# SQLite file. `:memory:` is supported for throwaway runs.
MENTAT_DB_PATH=./data/mentat.db

# Root directory for locally stored blobs.
MENTAT_BLOB_ROOT=./data/blobs

# Directory for generated local files (the master key lives here).
MENTAT_DATA_DIR=./data

# Maximum upload size, in bytes (default 50 MiB).
MENTAT_FILE_MAX_BYTES=52428800
```

## Secrets

```bash
# REQUIRED in production. 32 bytes as base64 (openssl rand -base64 32) or 64 hex.
# Omit locally and Mentat generates ./data/master.key on first use.
MENTAT_MASTER_KEY=

# Set these after a rotation so existing ciphertexts stay readable.
MENTAT_MASTER_KEY_PREVIOUS=
MENTAT_MASTER_KEY_VERSION=1
MENTAT_MASTER_KEY_PREVIOUS_VERSION=0
```

## Server

```bash
MENTAT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5273
MENTAT_LOG_LEVEL=info          # debug | info | warn | error
MENTAT_ALLOW_SIGNUP=true       # set false once accounts exist
MENTAT_SESSION_DAYS=30
MENTAT_COOKIE_SECURE=false     # true when served over HTTPS
```

## Worker

```bash
# In-process worker. Set false when running `bun run worker` separately.
MENTAT_WORKER_ENABLED=true
MENTAT_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4
MENTAT_WORKER_POLL_MS=500
# Lease duration. A worker that dies is recovered after this window.
MENTAT_JOB_LEASE_SECONDS=120
```

## Providers

```bash
# Prefilled URL in the provider setup form.
MENTAT_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
```

## Google Cloud Storage (optional)

Storage credentials are configured **per workspace** as a secret reference, not
here. The only environment variable involved is the standard Google client
configuration when you are not supplying a service-account JSON secret:

```bash
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json
# Optional default bucket suggestion.
MENTAT_GCS_BUCKET=
```

## Testing

```bash
# Playwright starts its own server; this only changes the port it uses.
MENTAT_E2E_PORT=5373
```
